1
00:00:02,052 --> 00:00:05,240
Crossing over mountains and through valleys

2
00:00:05,532 --> 00:00:08,899
A ninja flies freely through the sky just like a plane

3
00:00:09,065 --> 00:00:12,487
Honest and kind, Hattori-kun brings joy to everyone

4
00:00:12,605 --> 00:00:16,059
Opening eyes wide and keeping his little mouth shut tight

5
00:00:16,152 --> 00:00:19,520
Concealing his face with puffed-up cheeks

6
00:00:19,663 --> 00:00:23,040
Catching villains with agility fast as lightning

7
00:00:23,230 --> 00:00:26,400
Catching crooks with quirky moves just like magic tricks

8
00:00:27,037 --> 00:00:30,040
Speaking politely and proudly like poetry

9
00:00:31,508 --> 00:00:34,690
"Catching Big Fish in the Pond"

10
00:00:37,022 --> 00:00:39,513
Oh dear, where on earth did I put it?

11
00:00:39,564 --> 00:00:41,080
Ah, found it!

12
00:00:46,228 --> 00:00:47,948
What happened?

13
00:00:50,535 --> 00:00:52,821
So your family has a samurai sword too?

14
00:00:52,879 --> 00:00:54,522
A samurai sword?

15
00:00:55,328 --> 00:00:57,342
This is a fishing rod

16
00:00:58,374 --> 00:00:59,243
Wow, Kenichi

17
00:00:59,283 --> 00:01:01,526
This fishing rod looks really valuable

18
00:01:01,990 --> 00:01:05,321
Yeah, my grandpa used it for fishing when he was young

19
00:01:10,084 --> 00:01:12,568
Oh no, the fishing rod snapped!

20
00:01:12,810 --> 00:01:13,992
Don't worry

21
00:01:14,042 --> 00:01:16,908
I can make a new fishing rod for you

22
00:01:25,294 --> 00:01:27,311
This fishing rod is so nice

23
00:01:27,361 --> 00:01:30,223
Too bad I don't know how to fish at all

24
00:01:35,623 --> 00:01:39,203
Let me demonstrate how to fish properly

25
00:01:39,449 --> 00:01:40,127
Yumeko

26
00:01:40,167 --> 00:01:42,490
If you want to learn how to fish, I can teach you

27
00:01:43,831 --> 00:01:44,980
Oh, got a bite...

28
00:01:45,020 --> 00:01:47,200
You have to seize the moment

29
00:01:49,077 --> 00:01:50,458
Wow, I did it!

30
00:01:50,535 --> 00:01:51,932
Awesome, I finally caught one!

31
00:01:51,973 --> 00:01:54,223
Look, Yumeko, it's pretty big!

32
00:01:54,264 --> 00:01:56,894
Hey, Hattori-kun, you've got to step it up

33
00:01:56,935 --> 00:01:58,720
The more impatient you are, the less you'll catch

34
00:01:58,771 --> 00:02:00,443
Big Brother, there's a bite!

35
00:02:01,401 --> 00:02:02,505
Hurry up...

36
00:02:02,555 --> 00:02:04,771
The biggest mistake in fishing is being impatient

37
00:02:04,821 --> 00:02:06,440
Patience is what matters most

38
00:02:10,467 --> 00:02:12,966
Wow, it's so heavy! It must be a huge fish

39
00:02:13,215 --> 00:02:15,920
Let me help you, woah...

40
00:02:22,510 --> 00:02:24,660
How hilarious, you caught a tire!

41
00:02:32,220 --> 00:02:34,160
Looks like we got another bite

42
00:02:36,279 --> 00:02:38,333
Wow, Yumeko, you're a natural!

43
00:02:38,374 --> 00:02:40,080
You're an expert at fishing!

44
00:02:53,996 --> 00:02:56,640
Yumeko, look, another bite!

45
00:03:10,383 --> 00:03:12,559
Hey, Hattori-kun, you said you'd show me how to fish

46
00:03:12,609 --> 00:03:13,907
All you're catching is trash

47
00:03:13,957 --> 00:03:15,094
That's not fishing at all!

48
00:03:15,144 --> 00:03:16,466
That's really strange

49
00:03:16,516 --> 00:03:18,977
Maybe there's a problem with this fishing spot

50
00:03:20,364 --> 00:03:22,937
Look, I bet there are plenty of fish over there

51
00:03:27,475 --> 00:03:29,725
Woah, I can't take this... Ouch!

52
00:03:29,775 --> 00:03:31,395
Run! Ouch!

53
00:03:40,479 --> 00:03:42,629
Kenichi, this one's definitely a big fish!

54
00:03:42,670 --> 00:03:45,334
-Pull hard! One, two, three...
-Woah...

55
00:03:46,830 --> 00:03:49,603
Heave! Pull, pull hard...

56
00:03:55,779 --> 00:03:58,563
Oh well, never mind... Let me try fishing by myself

57
00:04:00,549 --> 00:04:03,156
Big Brother, things don't seem to be going well today

58
00:04:03,207 --> 00:04:04,603
Big Brother, look!

59
00:04:06,787 --> 00:04:08,011
Almost ready

60
00:04:10,136 --> 00:04:11,213
Unbelievable!

61
00:04:11,254 --> 00:04:12,377
So it was him playing tricks on us

62
00:04:12,417 --> 00:04:14,261
Kemumaki is awful!

63
00:04:18,122 --> 00:04:20,270
Yan...

64
00:04:20,320 --> 00:04:22,906
- Help!
- Yan...

65
00:04:24,038 --> 00:04:25,439
Help...

66
00:04:26,832 --> 00:04:28,045
Hey, don't run away!

67
00:04:28,096 --> 00:04:29,385
Unbelievable!

68
00:04:30,867 --> 00:04:32,519
Yan...

69
00:04:33,814 --> 00:04:35,923
Ah, so the reason Brother couldn't catch any fish

70
00:04:35,973 --> 00:04:38,657
was because Kagechiyo was playing tricks underwater

71
00:04:38,707 --> 00:04:39,998
All right

72
00:04:40,490 --> 00:04:41,553
This is really strange

73
00:04:41,603 --> 00:04:43,970
Why aren't we catching any fish at all now?

74
00:04:44,332 --> 00:04:45,401
Yeah, isn't it?

75
00:04:45,481 --> 00:04:47,379
Wonder what Kagechiyo is up to?

76
00:04:47,430 --> 00:04:48,575
Ah, it's so heavy!

77
00:04:48,710 --> 00:04:50,460
Stop moving, it's thrashing all over

78
00:04:50,511 --> 00:04:52,008
Oh no, stop...

79
00:04:52,059 --> 00:04:53,855
Hey, be good

80
00:05:02,555 --> 00:05:04,532
This fish must be huge

81
00:05:04,992 --> 00:05:06,169
They caught a big fish!

82
00:05:06,219 --> 00:05:08,499
I bet it's actually an old tire

83
00:05:09,081 --> 00:05:11,960
But this time, it really seems huge

84
00:05:12,266 --> 00:05:15,248
I don't think Kagechiyo would mess up this badly, right?

85
00:05:15,299 --> 00:05:17,196
Pull, pull hard!

86
00:05:24,586 --> 00:05:26,276
Whoa, did we really catch it?

87
00:05:27,241 --> 00:05:28,720
Yay, we caught it...

88
00:05:29,243 --> 00:05:29,976
Look at that

89
00:05:30,017 --> 00:05:32,791
Not only did we catch a fish, it's a huge one too!

90
00:05:33,913 --> 00:05:36,163
Kenichi, you're amazing!

91
00:05:40,122 --> 00:05:42,880
Wow, how did you catch such a big fish?

92
00:05:42,931 --> 00:05:43,750
Look at it

93
00:05:43,800 --> 00:05:46,376
This proves my fishing skills are pretty good

94
00:05:46,427 --> 00:05:48,785
When Dad sees you caught such a big fish

95
00:05:48,835 --> 00:05:50,107
he'll definitely be thrilled

96
00:05:50,666 --> 00:05:52,850
Can a fish that big really be in the pond though?

97
00:05:54,024 --> 00:05:55,468
Thank you very much for your business

98
00:05:55,518 --> 00:05:56,554
I'm the fishmonger

99
00:05:56,610 --> 00:05:58,450
I'm here to collect payment for that big fish

100
00:05:58,501 --> 00:05:59,797
Huh? Collect payment?

101
00:05:59,848 --> 00:06:00,566
That's right

102
00:06:00,606 --> 00:06:02,669
I sell fish on the next street over

103
00:06:02,710 --> 00:06:04,285
Your young master is quite impressive

104
00:06:04,335 --> 00:06:07,282
He's so small, but he still managed to carry such a huge fish

105
00:06:08,588 --> 00:06:10,995
Oh, so it was Shinzo causing trouble

106
00:06:11,046 --> 00:06:12,914
Where did he run off to?

107
00:06:12,964 --> 00:06:13,497
Just you wait

108
00:06:13,554 --> 00:06:15,434
When he gets back, I'm definitely teaching him a lesson

109
00:06:15,484 --> 00:06:16,570
Shinzo!

110
00:06:21,684 --> 00:06:24,730
Luckily I learned the ninja swimming technique!

111
00:06:28,783 --> 00:06:31,663
"Who Is the Owner?"

112
00:06:41,058 --> 00:06:43,145
This eraser belongs to him

113
00:06:44,658 --> 00:06:47,598
All right, now open your books to page 38

114
00:06:47,649 --> 00:06:48,789
Excuse me, Teacher

115
00:06:48,839 --> 00:06:49,920
Kemumaki, what is it?

116
00:06:50,937 --> 00:06:53,377
I just found an eraser

117
00:06:53,904 --> 00:06:54,934
Oh, right

118
00:06:54,990 --> 00:06:56,100
Handling lost items

119
00:06:56,140 --> 00:06:57,787
is the job of the student on duty

120
00:06:57,837 --> 00:06:59,700
By the way, who is on duty this week?

121
00:06:59,757 --> 00:07:01,275
Teacher, it's me

122
00:07:01,382 --> 00:07:04,360
Alright, go find the owner and return the eraser to them

123
00:07:04,492 --> 00:07:05,275
Yes, sir

124
00:07:05,382 --> 00:07:08,520
Excuse me, did anyone lose an eraser?

125
00:07:12,073 --> 00:07:13,156
This is completely absurd

126
00:07:13,206 --> 00:07:13,990
Kids these days

127
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:15,847
don't take care of their belongings at all

128
00:07:15,897 --> 00:07:17,812
They don't look after them properly

129
00:07:17,862 --> 00:07:19,465
This kind of attitude is unacceptable

130
00:07:19,515 --> 00:07:20,400
They really need a scolding

131
00:07:21,009 --> 00:07:22,963
Monitor, on that eraser...

132
00:07:23,004 --> 00:07:24,422
is there an owner's name?

133
00:07:24,473 --> 00:07:25,483
A name?

134
00:07:25,861 --> 00:07:26,680
Let me see

135
00:07:27,219 --> 00:07:28,349
Ah, Teacher!

136
00:07:28,399 --> 00:07:29,949
I found a name on it

137
00:07:29,999 --> 00:07:31,022
It says Ken

138
00:07:31,072 --> 00:07:33,498
Which of you is Ken? Step forward

139
00:07:34,030 --> 00:07:34,921
Teacher

140
00:07:34,985 --> 00:07:35,942
In our class

141
00:07:35,982 --> 00:07:38,075
there's only one student named Ken

142
00:07:38,848 --> 00:07:40,958
That's right, I'm the only Ken

143
00:07:41,142 --> 00:07:42,815
The eraser is mine

144
00:07:44,269 --> 00:07:44,991
Ridiculous!

145
00:07:45,042 --> 00:07:47,579
Not even recognising your own belongings is outrageous

146
00:07:47,629 --> 00:07:50,269
Wait, but there wasn't a name on my eraser

147
00:07:50,320 --> 00:07:53,230
Someone must have written my name on it on purpose

148
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:54,181
Is that so?

149
00:07:54,232 --> 00:07:56,363
I swear to God!

150
00:07:56,725 --> 00:07:57,549
Alright

151
00:07:57,599 --> 00:07:59,201
I'm always telling you

152
00:07:59,251 --> 00:08:00,554
to write your names on your belongings

153
00:08:00,604 --> 00:08:01,581
and you never do

154
00:08:01,631 --> 00:08:02,725
You're directly disobeying my orders

155
00:08:02,766 --> 00:08:03,738
Well, uh...

156
00:08:04,017 --> 00:08:06,029
Hmph, you're completely hopeless!

157
00:08:09,410 --> 00:08:12,093
These are all the lost items that have piled up since April

158
00:08:12,137 --> 00:08:13,860
No one ever came to claim them

159
00:08:13,917 --> 00:08:15,230
so they just kept piling up

160
00:08:15,280 --> 00:08:16,930
Treating your belongings so carelessly

161
00:08:16,980 --> 00:08:18,500
is really crossing the line

162
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:20,203
If I'm not mistaken

163
00:08:20,254 --> 00:08:22,303
every single one of these items must be yours, Kenichi

164
00:08:22,353 --> 00:08:24,188
No way, no matter how careless I am...

165
00:08:24,238 --> 00:08:26,308
- I'd never leave behind this much stuff!
- Alright, you have this week

166
00:08:26,358 --> 00:08:27,549
to finish this task

167
00:08:27,599 --> 00:08:28,649
You must track down the owners

168
00:08:28,700 --> 00:08:30,755
for every single one of these lost items

169
00:08:30,805 --> 00:08:32,762
and return everything to them

170
00:08:32,812 --> 00:08:34,694
Return them to their rightful owners, got it?

171
00:08:34,834 --> 00:08:36,086
Teacher, that's unfair!

172
00:08:36,127 --> 00:08:38,398
That task is basically impossible

173
00:08:38,448 --> 00:08:41,215
In that case, I'll just assume you lost every single one of them

174
00:08:41,955 --> 00:08:43,848
Ugh, this is infuriating!

175
00:08:45,170 --> 00:08:47,150
And that's what happened

176
00:08:47,201 --> 00:08:48,445
So that's how it is

177
00:08:48,486 --> 00:08:50,709
Kenichi, I sympathise with what you're going through

178
00:08:50,750 --> 00:08:52,651
That's why I don't want to go to school

179
00:08:52,701 --> 00:08:54,225
Having to find all the owners...

180
00:08:54,275 --> 00:08:55,685
That's completely impossible

181
00:08:55,735 --> 00:08:57,458
In an Iga ninja's dictionary

182
00:08:57,509 --> 00:08:59,129
There's no such thing as "impossible"

183
00:08:59,202 --> 00:09:00,500
Can you really do it?

184
00:09:00,551 --> 00:09:02,372
That's right, I'll get started right away

185
00:09:02,429 --> 00:09:04,263
Oh, you're my savior!

186
00:09:04,313 --> 00:09:06,240
I don't know how to repay you!

187
00:09:08,536 --> 00:09:10,052
Yan...

188
00:09:10,712 --> 00:09:12,480
Yan...

189
00:09:14,672 --> 00:09:16,957
Kenichi, is it this classroom?

190
00:09:28,377 --> 00:09:30,016
Ow, that hurts!

191
00:09:30,056 --> 00:09:31,755
Ouch, that really hurts!

192
00:09:31,796 --> 00:09:32,917
Yan!

193
00:09:35,044 --> 00:09:36,457
Yan...

194
00:09:36,784 --> 00:09:38,247
Yan...

195
00:09:38,298 --> 00:09:39,600
- Is it this box?
- Mm-hmm

196
00:09:43,630 --> 00:09:45,296
Why are there so many lost items?

197
00:09:45,576 --> 00:09:47,063
If I lost something

198
00:09:47,114 --> 00:09:49,059
And someone found it for me, I'd definitely thank them

199
00:09:49,100 --> 00:09:50,887
And claim my belongings

200
00:09:50,937 --> 00:09:54,920
It's a shame the kids don't cherish their things at all

201
00:09:55,141 --> 00:09:57,478
Don't lecture me like a teacher!

202
00:09:57,519 --> 00:09:59,280
Sorry, I didn't mean to

203
00:09:59,860 --> 00:10:00,832
Enough talk

204
00:10:00,883 --> 00:10:02,783
You said you had a way to find all the owners

205
00:10:02,833 --> 00:10:03,751
Is that really true?

206
00:10:03,792 --> 00:10:04,949
Mm, trust me

207
00:10:04,999 --> 00:10:06,580
As expected of an Iga ninja!

208
00:10:06,620 --> 00:10:09,342
No, I won't be using ninjutsu

209
00:10:09,852 --> 00:10:11,345
This is very simple

210
00:10:11,386 --> 00:10:13,220
No ninjutsu needed, don't worry

211
00:10:13,260 --> 00:10:14,660
Ah, that's it!

212
00:10:14,710 --> 00:10:17,313
I've got it! I have a great idea too

213
00:10:17,402 --> 00:10:18,472
It's super simple

214
00:10:18,512 --> 00:10:20,638
All we have to do is write Kemumaki's name on them

215
00:10:24,556 --> 00:10:26,121
This is the best way!

216
00:10:26,728 --> 00:10:27,693
You can't do that!

217
00:10:27,733 --> 00:10:29,760
Because that goes against ninja ethics!

218
00:10:29,805 --> 00:10:32,361
I just want to get back at Kemumaki, that's all

219
00:10:32,412 --> 00:10:33,989
I sympathize with you

220
00:10:34,039 --> 00:10:35,518
But for now, I just need to find

221
00:10:35,558 --> 00:10:37,269
The owner of every single item

222
00:10:37,319 --> 00:10:38,550
Let's not do anything else

223
00:10:38,590 --> 00:10:39,622
I got it

224
00:10:39,673 --> 00:10:40,369
All right, Kenichi

225
00:10:40,419 --> 00:10:41,959
Let's come back tomorrow, okay?

226
00:10:42,010 --> 00:10:44,600
Aw, why are you being like this?

227
00:10:45,179 --> 00:10:46,144
It won't work

228
00:10:46,184 --> 00:10:48,939
If the whole class isn't here, I can't succeed

229
00:10:50,760 --> 00:10:52,932
Hey, why did you have to climb through the window?

230
00:10:52,983 --> 00:10:54,760
That's what makes it feel like a ninja, you know

231
00:10:55,550 --> 00:10:56,670
You're driving me crazy!

232
00:10:59,061 --> 00:11:00,500
Huh? You're saying Hattori-kun

233
00:11:00,540 --> 00:11:02,480
Has a way to find all the owners?

234
00:11:02,661 --> 00:11:04,117
That's right, which is why

235
00:11:04,158 --> 00:11:06,076
I asked Hattori-kun to help today

236
00:11:06,126 --> 00:11:07,843
Hattori-kun, are you ready?

237
00:11:07,893 --> 00:11:09,261
Absolutely no problem!

238
00:11:10,533 --> 00:11:11,423
Shishimaru!

239
00:11:15,403 --> 00:11:16,543
Ready?

240
00:11:28,123 --> 00:11:30,143
This pen is mine!

241
00:11:30,303 --> 00:11:31,503
-Yay...
-Yay...

242
00:11:31,554 --> 00:11:32,735
Yay me...

243
00:11:32,776 --> 00:11:34,600
I won't let you praise yourself!

244
00:11:40,242 --> 00:11:41,635
That triangle ruler is mine

245
00:11:41,864 --> 00:11:42,791
Great...

246
00:11:49,249 --> 00:11:50,830
Teacher, this is all that's left

247
00:11:50,894 --> 00:11:52,674
So we couldn't find all the owners after all?

248
00:11:52,718 --> 00:11:53,708
Ah, that's right

249
00:11:54,154 --> 00:11:56,423
Then this dog's performance was only so-so

250
00:11:56,464 --> 00:11:58,266
How awful, insulting me like that!

251
00:12:02,969 --> 00:12:05,080
Ow, hey...

252
00:12:08,302 --> 00:12:11,341
Teacher, please have them look closely at these items first

253
00:12:12,692 --> 00:12:14,278
Oh, are they all mine?

254
00:12:14,328 --> 00:12:15,645
Teacher, that's awful!

255
00:12:15,695 --> 00:12:18,611
People lately really don't
take care of their belongings

256
00:12:21,229 --> 00:12:23,372
That's the pot calling the kettle black!

257
00:12:26,638 --> 00:12:29,928
"Dad, Please Come Home Early"

258
00:12:50,925 --> 00:12:52,122
I'm home

259
00:13:02,526 --> 00:13:03,479
You're back?

260
00:13:03,520 --> 00:13:05,536
Yes, I'm home now

261
00:13:06,655 --> 00:13:08,370
Why are you back so late?

262
00:13:08,578 --> 00:13:10,582
I... I ate dinner before coming home

263
00:13:10,758 --> 00:13:12,697
Now, let me help you tidy up

264
00:13:14,023 --> 00:13:15,682
No need to help, I can tidy up myself

265
00:13:15,948 --> 00:13:17,318
Do you know what time it is?

266
00:13:17,368 --> 00:13:19,729
Can't you come home a bit earlier?

267
00:13:20,688 --> 00:13:21,721
Except on Sundays

268
00:13:21,761 --> 00:13:23,840
the family never gets to eat together during the week

269
00:13:23,891 --> 00:13:25,449
Oh dear, I know

270
00:13:25,499 --> 00:13:27,782
I have a good reason for being late, *sigh*

271
00:13:27,832 --> 00:13:29,693
You always have so many excuses

272
00:13:30,573 --> 00:13:31,411
Hattori-kun

273
00:13:31,571 --> 00:13:32,836
Hattori-kun

274
00:13:32,916 --> 00:13:34,250
Wake up quickly!

275
00:13:34,515 --> 00:13:36,600
Yan...

276
00:13:38,015 --> 00:13:39,754
I was already awake

277
00:13:39,805 --> 00:13:41,588
I heard you snoring

278
00:13:41,673 --> 00:13:44,264
This way of sleeping is a type of ninjutsu

279
00:13:44,347 --> 00:13:46,664
-Speaking of our Iga style ninjutsu...
-Alright...

280
00:13:46,715 --> 00:13:48,247
No need to explain so much

281
00:13:48,298 --> 00:13:50,896
I know you can do anything, so show it with your actions

282
00:13:50,947 --> 00:13:53,605
Oh dear, I have a bad feeling about this

283
00:13:53,656 --> 00:13:55,735
Kenichi, what do you need me to do?

284
00:13:55,785 --> 00:13:57,951
Well, my dad comes home very late every night

285
00:13:58,017 --> 00:13:59,634
Make him come home earlier

286
00:13:59,685 --> 00:14:01,500
Yan...

287
00:14:10,602 --> 00:14:12,122
Mm... thanks for your hard work

288
00:14:12,189 --> 00:14:13,589
Yan...

289
00:14:13,639 --> 00:14:14,840
Yan...

290
00:14:21,105 --> 00:14:23,422
I should be able to go home early today

291
00:14:25,363 --> 00:14:27,120
I'm really sorry

292
00:14:28,625 --> 00:14:31,683
But we have to finish
these documents today

293
00:14:31,734 --> 00:14:33,830
Like this, you just need to stamp them

294
00:14:33,881 --> 00:14:35,266
Uh... let me do it

295
00:14:35,317 --> 00:14:36,560
Thanks so much for your help

296
00:14:39,891 --> 00:14:43,333
It'll take at least three hours to stamp them all, let me make a phone call first

297
00:14:45,220 --> 00:14:46,274
Hello, who is this?

298
00:14:46,495 --> 00:14:47,680
Oh, honey

299
00:14:47,811 --> 00:14:50,000
I'm really sorry tonight, I... uh...

300
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:52,800
This technique is called "Ninja Possession"

301
00:14:55,211 --> 00:14:57,420
Yan...

302
00:15:03,105 --> 00:15:05,207
What's wrong, Dad? What's going on?

303
00:15:12,956 --> 00:15:14,032
That's really strange

304
00:15:14,082 --> 00:15:15,000
Why is that? Hey

305
00:15:15,107 --> 00:15:16,407
What are you talking about?

306
00:15:16,457 --> 00:15:17,892
Are you coming home for dinner or not?

307
00:15:17,943 --> 00:15:19,184
Answer me quickly!

308
00:15:19,408 --> 00:15:20,665
I'm definitely coming home for dinner

309
00:15:20,706 --> 00:15:22,317
Remember to cook my portion too

310
00:15:22,368 --> 00:15:23,867
Really? Well, all right then

311
00:15:23,918 --> 00:15:26,200
I'll cook a few of my specialties

312
00:15:28,500 --> 00:15:29,509
*sigh* That really is strange

313
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:32,634
How could I have stamped everything
in the blink of an eye?

315
00:15:33,573 --> 00:15:35,118
Hey, you haven't left yet?

316
00:15:35,995 --> 00:15:37,165
What's up?

317
00:15:37,206 --> 00:15:38,196
It's only five o'clock

318
00:15:38,236 --> 00:15:40,668
How about we grab a drink before going home?

319
00:15:40,727 --> 00:15:42,544
Huh? Ah, go for a drink?

320
00:15:45,568 --> 00:15:46,697
Have another drink!

321
00:15:46,944 --> 00:15:48,460
Thanks a lot

322
00:15:49,961 --> 00:15:52,047
Yan...

323
00:15:56,322 --> 00:15:58,247
Yan...

324
00:16:03,022 --> 00:16:04,922
Yan...

325
00:16:08,959 --> 00:16:12,477
Why did I get drunk so fast today?

326
00:16:17,077 --> 00:16:18,446
Man, I don't know why

327
00:16:18,486 --> 00:16:20,794
I was so efficient at work today!

328
00:16:20,845 --> 00:16:22,300
That's great

329
00:16:22,340 --> 00:16:23,702
Though I'm really sorry

330
00:16:23,752 --> 00:16:25,834
Because you came home especially early today

331
00:16:25,891 --> 00:16:27,936
I haven't finished cooking dinner yet

332
00:16:28,004 --> 00:16:28,832
Oh, that's fine

333
00:16:28,972 --> 00:16:31,607
Let me cook a couple of dishes myself tonight

334
00:16:31,694 --> 00:16:33,015
Oh? You're going into the kitchen?

335
00:16:33,066 --> 00:16:35,083
Don't worry, leave it to me!

336
00:16:38,867 --> 00:16:40,684
My stomach is growling

337
00:16:42,868 --> 00:16:45,426
Hey, dinner is ready, come out and eat!

338
00:16:46,037 --> 00:16:46,880
Coming!

339
00:16:58,150 --> 00:16:58,950
All right

340
00:16:59,175 --> 00:17:01,011
Let me try the first bite

341
00:17:05,438 --> 00:17:07,267
Oh no, why is it so salty? Oh dear

342
00:17:07,318 --> 00:17:09,051
I used salt instead of sugar

343
00:17:09,125 --> 00:17:10,318
*sigh* Better cook it again from scratch

344
00:17:11,622 --> 00:17:13,390
Oh dear, Mom...

345
00:17:22,130 --> 00:17:24,626
Dad, let me do my homework myself

346
00:17:24,667 --> 00:17:26,059
Hold on, stop making noise

347
00:17:26,100 --> 00:17:27,680
I don't know why, but I feel like

348
00:17:27,730 --> 00:17:29,668
your math homework lately is really hard to solve

349
00:17:29,718 --> 00:17:30,200
That's right

350
00:17:30,251 --> 00:17:32,760
I don't even know whether to multiply or divide now

351
00:17:33,003 --> 00:17:34,450
Ugh, let me do the math myself!

352
00:17:34,501 --> 00:17:35,598
Stop fussing

353
00:17:35,648 --> 00:17:37,200
Kenichi, go play outside

354
00:17:37,294 --> 00:17:39,777
I won't let you get in the way of someone working

355
00:17:39,818 --> 00:17:42,027
Man, this is so frustrating!

356
00:17:48,326 --> 00:17:50,449
Let me help you tally up the numbers, okay?

357
00:17:50,500 --> 00:17:52,240
No need, I can count it myself

358
00:17:53,969 --> 00:17:55,926
Dad, what are you doing now?

359
00:17:56,363 --> 00:17:57,773
We need to make breakfast tomorrow morning

360
00:17:57,823 --> 00:17:59,440
I'll go wash the rice first

361
00:17:59,490 --> 00:18:00,642
No need

362
00:18:00,762 --> 00:18:02,182
I've had quite enough of you

364
00:18:02,718 --> 00:18:04,323
If you're home early, don't get in the way

365
00:18:04,364 --> 00:18:05,850
Hattori, starting tomorrow...

366
00:18:04,833 --> 00:18:05,901
{\an8}I was only trying to help

367
00:18:05,959 --> 00:18:08,181
I want Dad to come home late like he used to

363
00:18:05,982 --> 00:18:08,110
{\an8}-Oh no, the more Dad tries to help, the worse it gets
-You're lying!

369
00:18:08,751 --> 00:18:10,547
-You're being completely unreasonable
-Let me tell you

370
00:18:10,588 --> 00:18:11,700
-He can even convey that?
-No help is better than this!

371
00:18:11,741 --> 00:18:12,957
Well, since you put it that way...

368
00:18:11,953 --> 00:18:12,873
{\an8}You can't be serious

372
00:18:13,007 --> 00:18:16,193
How about I use ninjutsu
to make him come home later?

373
00:18:13,233 --> 00:18:15,900
{\an8}You came home and just started messing things up

374
00:18:16,453 --> 00:18:17,340
Aiya!

375
00:18:17,380 --> 00:18:21,277
This story teaches us
that nothing in this world is perfect

